  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two long parallel wires P and Q are a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"d\"></span> apart. They each carry a current.</p>\n<p>A magnetic force per unit length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span> acts on P due to Q.</p>\n<p>The distance between the wires is increased to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2d\"></span> and the current in Q is decreased to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{I}{2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure><br/>What is the magnetic force per unit length that acts on P due to Q after the changes?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F}{8}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F}{4}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F}{2}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
